From: Avocado Linux <info@avocadolinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/tegra: fbdev: take the core-allocated fb_info when the allocator is private

linux-yocto 6.6.151 carries the stable backport that moves fb_info
allocation into the fbdev core: __drm_fb_helper_initial_config_and_unlock()
allocates helper->info before calling the driver's fb_probe, and
drm_fb_helper_alloc_info() became static in drm_fb_helper.c. The in-tree
tegra driver now just reads helper->info.

The OOT driver chose between drm_fb_helper_alloc_info() (Linux v6.2+)
and drm_fb_helper_alloc_fbi() (older) only. With the first now private,
the conftest reports it absent and the build falls through to the
pre-6.2 name, which no longer exists either:

    fbdev.c:129:16: error: implicit declaration of function
    'drm_fb_helper_alloc_fbi'

Add a middle case keyed on the existing NV_DRM_FB_HELPER_STRUCT_HAS_INFO_ARG
conftest (struct drm_fb_helper has .info, Linux v6.2+): when the
allocator is not exported there, the core has already allocated
fb_info, so take helper->info. Kernels that still export the allocator
keep using it, and pre-6.2 kernels keep drm_fb_helper_alloc_fbi(). Probed
rather than version-checked because it arrived as a stable backport.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fbdev.c
+++ b/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fbdev.c
@@ -125,6 +125,13 @@
 
 #if defined(NV_DRM_FB_HELPER_ALLOC_INFO_PRESENT) /* Linux v6.2 */
 	info = drm_fb_helper_alloc_info(helper);
+#elif defined(NV_DRM_FB_HELPER_STRUCT_HAS_INFO_ARG) /* allocated by the core */
+	/*
+	 * The fbdev core allocates fb_info before calling the probe and made
+	 * drm_fb_helper_alloc_info() static; the in-tree driver takes
+	 * helper->info the same way.
+	 */
+	info = helper->info;
 #else
 	info = drm_fb_helper_alloc_fbi(helper);
 #endif
